Write $sigma_1$ as disjoint cycles $mat(a^i_1, ..., a^i_(l_i))$. If $sigma_2$ has the same cycle type, write its corresponding cycles as $mat(b^i_1, ..., b^i_(l_i))$ and define $tau(a^i_j)=b^i_j$. Then $tau sigma_1 tau^(-1)=sigma_2$.

Conversely, if $sigma_2=tau sigma_1 tau^(-1)$, replacing each $a^i_j$ by $b^i_j=tau(a^i_j)$ gives a disjoint-cycle expression for $sigma_2$ with the same cycle lengths as $sigma_1$.
